      <div class="origin-copy reveal" data-reveal style="transition-delay:.1s">
        <p>Candor Digital didn't start with a pitch deck. It started with a simple rule: never claim a result we can't actually show someone. Every idea gets tested on a real brand first, the numbers get watched closely, and only what genuinely moves them becomes part of how we work — before any of it turns into a service worth paying for.</p>
        <p>That's still how this practice operates. Small, provable moves before big claims. A short trial before a long contract. A straight answer before a sales pitch. Not because "candor" sounded like a good brand word — but because it's the only way a new, small practice earns the right to charge for its opinion.</p>
        <p class="origin-line">So here's the candid version of our own pitch: <span>we're new, we're small on purpose, and every result on this site from here on will be one we can actually show you — not one we're asking you to take on faith.</span></p>
      </div>
